                  "policy_refs": [
                    "question-participation@1",
                    "review-applicability@1",
                    "waiver-applicability@1"
                  ]
                },
                "body": "# Command-line calculator product intent\n\n## Decision\n\nBuild a command-line calculator. Invoke it as `calculator <left> <operator> <right>`. Support only the operators `+`, `-`, `*`, and `/`. Accept operands matching exactly `[+-]?(?:[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]*)?|\\.[0-9]+)`. Emit canonical successful output. For nonterminating results, round exactly at the 12th fractional digit using half-away-from-zero and then trim. For invalid input, emit no stdout, emit exactly `invalid input\\n` on stderr, and exit 2. For division by zero, emit no stdout, emit exactly `division by zero\\n` on stderr, and exit 2.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe attended stakeholder explicitly selected this product behavior and its command-line, operand, operator, output, rounding, and error-handling boundaries.\n\n## Alternatives\n\nNone recorded.\n\n## Effective scope\n\n`$proposal.updatedQuestion.revision_id`\n"
              }
            }
          ],
